# Incremental Source Organizer

Read input.json. It contains {{ new_source_count }} `new_sources`, previously ungrouped Source summaries, and cached
Groups with compact member summaries. Source and Group refs are Runtime-owned handles. Existing Group membership is
fixed in this stage and must not be repeated, moved, merged, or reconsidered.

Review the input through projections below 12,000 characters containing Source refs, Providers, titles, summaries,
and only the identity metadata needed for grouping. Complete every projection before deciding.

Write decision.json with exactly {"groups":[...],"ungrouped":["S001"]}. Every ref in `new_sources` must appear exactly
once. A previously ungrouped ref may appear only when the new evidence now proves a Group; otherwise omit it.

To add refs to one cached Group, write only {"group_ref":"G001","members":["S001"]}. The Runtime preserves the cached
title, identity, and existing members. To create a new Group, write title, identity, and members without group_ref;
Runtime allocates its durable ID. Never invent Source refs, Group refs, IDs, hashes, schema versions, or paths.

A Group has one purpose: combine records that are direct representations of the same canonical research object.
Members usually come from different Providers, but two records from one Provider qualify when they are release
variants of the same object, such as the size variants of one model release line. Group only when the metadata
identifies one exact named project, model release line, paper and its explicitly identified implementation, dataset,
benchmark, or other canonical object.

Direct representations may include an official project repository, its official model repository or release variants,
its primary paper, and a repository explicitly identified as the implementation of that exact paper. The Group title
and identity must name that one canonical object.

Keep records separate when their relationship is only any of the following: built on, based on, adapted from,
fine-tuned from, compatible with, inspired by, shares an architecture, belongs to a broad model family, addresses the
same task, or provides a third-party integration or toolkit. A separately named derivative remains a separate Source.
Do not create umbrella families or dependency groups. When identity is uncertain, put the Source ref in ungrouped.

Each final Group must contain at least two Sources. Use one of these exact shapes and no other fields:

{
  "title": "human-readable canonical object",
  "identity": "concise rule proving every member is a direct representation of that object",
  "members": ["S001", "S002"],
}

{"group_ref":"G001","members":["S001"]}

Use only the compact metadata already present in input.json. Original Provider files and Provider interfaces are not
mounted in this workspace. This is a single-Agent stage: do not call rlm or spawn children. Do not search or download
anything. After writing decision.json call `submit_organizer_decision()`; when it reports a validation error, repair the same
file and call it again. Complete only after that Tool succeeds.
